  "limits": "Complete 625-frame Eiger9M warm-cache read/decode to stored-orientation uint32 consumer; no masking, float conversion, normalization or integration. Raw file reads, decompression, worker/buffer creation, source checks and delivery are timed. Opening/chunk indexing, interpreter startup and SHA256 validation are excluded. Fresh process and workers per pass, one reusable output per worker; both readers dynamically assign frame indices to fixed worker loops without a decoded-frame queue. Each implementation/worker count first validates all 625 frames against the independent h5py/HDF5 reference; those full passes also warm the file cache. Native uses bounded lz4_flex plus Bitshuffle; Jon uses his installed package's LZ4 and public default KCB API. jon-neon is an explicitly selected private native entry-point diagnostic with the same per-frame buffer policy. Native compressed buffers are reusable; os.pread returns new bytes for Python. Each API's required overheads are included. Host not reserved; background load recorded, no cold-disk claim.",
